        <h1>🐍 Complete Python 3 Quick Formula Handbook</h1>
        <p><strong>Chief Mentor:</strong> Rohit Sir | <strong>Helpline:</strong> 9509934266 | <strong>Batch:</strong> Daily 02:00 PM</p>
        
        <h2>1. Variables & Data Types</h2>
        <pre># Python Dynamic Typing
name = "Rohit Sir"       # str
age = 25                # int
fees = 299.00           # float
is_vip = True           # bool</pre>

        <h2>2. Operators Quick Reference</h2>
        <table>
            <tr><th>Operator</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th><th>Result</th></tr>
            <tr><td><code>//</code></td><td>Floor Division</td><td><code>7 // 2</code></td><td><code>3</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>**</code></td><td>Exponent (Power)</td><td><code>2 ** 3</code></td><td><code>8</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>%</code></td><td>Modulus (Remainder)</td><td><code>7 % 2</code></td><td><code>1</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>in</code></td><td>Membership</td><td><code>'py' in 'python'</code></td><td><code>True</code></td></tr>
        </table>

        <h2>3. Lists & Dictionaries</h2>
        <pre># List Operations
skills = ["Python", "Flask", "Django", "SQL"]
skills.append("AI")
print(skills[0:2]) # ['Python', 'Flask']

# Dictionary Operations
student = {"name": "Aman", "city": "Kuchaman City", "xp": 850}
print(student.get("city")) # 'Kuchaman City'</pre>

        <h2>4. Functions & Lambda</h2>
        <pre># Def Function
def greet(student_name):
    return f"नमस्ते {student_name}! Welcome to Python Sikho."

# Lambda One-Liner
square = lambda x: x * x
print(square(9)) # 81</pre>

